   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>
                        <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">RECEIVED</seg> TWENTYFIVE POUNDS THANKS <name type="person" key="joyc82">JOYCE</name>
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">
                    <p>On <date when="1916-01-12">12 January 1916</date>, Ezra Pound had written to Harriet Shaw Weaver: “I have just had a desperate letter from Joyce. He has ‘answered 60 newspaper ads.’ etc. etc. NO work. If you haven’t already written to him, can you send him £5. at once, as a loan, as advance payment, as anything?” (British Library, Add. MS 57345, pp. 25, 26). On <date when="1916-01-14">14 January 1916</date>, Weaver wrote to JJ: “Meantime, as our journal, after stringent economics, is now in a better financial position than it was when your novel was running through it, we think it only fair to make you some payment for the past serial rights, &amp; we could now pay you £50” (Firth 156).</p>
                    <p>JJ thanks Harriet Weaver more extensively in his <rs type="letter" key="L_68280">letter of <date when="1916-02-05">5 February 1916</date>
                        </rs>.</p>
                </note>
            </div>
      </body>
